  "defect_record": {
    "defect_id": "EVAL-DEFECT-001",
    "effect_on_comparison": "NONE. The defect suppressed one problem identically in all seven arms, so every paired difference is unchanged. It understated ABSOLUTE accuracy in every arm by the same 1/15.",
    "fix": "rescore() now re-derives answer_correct and extracted_answer from the stored raw output via check_answer, exactly as it already re-derived the encoding score. Raw model output is never modified.",
    "found_at": "after arm-level generation-0 results were viewed under EVAL_SPEC_v1.0",
    "found_how": "Manual inspection of the two problems every arm failed. All seven arms had in fact produced a correct dimension for d24_unknown_constant; the scorer marked all seven wrong.",
    "protocol_note": "Per the directive, a defect found after viewing comparative results does not permit a silent scorer edit. The v1.0 result is preserved verbatim, this record documents the defect, and the stored raw outputs are transparently rescored under EVAL_SPEC_v1.1.",
    "root_cause": "Answer correctness was computed once, at trial time, and evaluation/analyse.py::rescore re-derived only the ENCODING score. The trial-time parse_dimension could not read a parenthesised denominator such as 'Mass * Length^2 / (Time^2 * Temperature)'. That parser was fixed before the freeze, but the stored answer verdicts were never re-derived, so the fix did not reach them.",
    "scope_of_effect": "7 of 105 generation-0 cells, all on problem d24_unknown_constant, exactly one per arm, all changing False -> True.",
    "v1_0_headline": "A 86.7, A_prime 86.7, B 86.7, C 80.0, D 86.7, E 86.7, F 86.7; every paired difference zero except D-vs-C +0.067 (McNemar p=1.0).",
    "v1_0_result_preserved_at": [
      "evaluation/results/EVAL_SPEC_v1.0.PRESERVED.json",
      "evaluation/results/eval001-gen0.analysis.EVAL_SPEC_v1.0.PRESERVED.json"
    ]
  },
  "eval_spec_version": "EVAL_SPEC_v1.1",
  "frozen_at_utc": "2026-08-05T13:29:16+01:00",
  "information_asymmetry": [
    "Arms D/E/F carry a ~90-line specification of a language invented weeks ago. Arm C names Stan and Lean, which the model saw extensively in pretraining and needs no specification for. This is the out-of-distribution confound and prompt construction cannot remove it. Direction: against the Hamiltonian arms.",
    "Arms D/E/F therefore have a longer prompt than arms A/A'/B. Prompt tokens are recorded per call so the difference is measured rather than assumed away. Direction: raises Hamiltonian cost, does not affect its accuracy.",
    "Arm E receives compiler diagnostics that no other arm receives. This is the experimental condition under test (H4), not an accident, and arm D is the matched control for it.",
    "Arm A' receives an explicit reasoning schema that arms B and C do not. A' is the control for scaffolding, so scaffolding is deliberately confounded with A' alone.",
    "The model under test is a reasoning model: it decomposes problems internally in every arm. This compresses the A-to-A' difference and therefore inflates any A'-to-Hamiltonian difference. Direction: in favour of the Hamiltonian arms."
  ],
